# Release number for the whole app.
#
# BUMP THIS ON EVERY RELEASE - including one that changes no browser file at
# all, such as a PHP fix or a docs fix. That is the point of this file:
#
#   VERSION                  -> this number. Moves on ANY release.
#   ui/js/store.js           -> APP_VERSION. The browser cache-buster; moves
#                               only when a file the browser caches changes.
#
# The update check at Config -> Updates reads BOTH from the published copy and
# announces a release when either is newer than this copy's. Before this file
# existed the check could only see the cache-buster, so a release that changed
# PHP and left the browser files alone was invisible and reported as "up to
# date" - the failure this file exists to remove.
#
# Rules:
#   * a PLAIN INTEGER, no dots - the comparison is numeric, so "2026.10.26"
#     would never read as newer.
#   * only ever increase.
#   * the first non-comment line is the number; blank lines and lines starting
#     with # or // are ignored, which is why this comment can live here.
#
# A copy with no readable number here still works: the check falls back to the
# cache-buster, exactly as it did before.
#
# The full routine, including the three places APP_VERSION has to change
# together, is in RELEASING.md next to this file.
350
